From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 20:40:57 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] vrend: ignore a plane number that a texture cannot honour

A guest resource that is the second or a later plane of an image sends the
plane number in the word of a sampler view that holds the first and last
layer, so the first layer comes out past the last. Only a resource that holds
the planes of an image, an imported buffer with auxiliary plane images, has
anything to select with it. A guest that takes the planes of an NV12 picture
from separate buffers samples a texture of its own for each, and the second
one failed its sampler view for having no layers, which failed the whole
command buffer and left the picture unsampled.

Read such a plane as the whole texture unless the resource has the plane's
image.
---
 src/vrend/vrend_renderer.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/vrend/vrend_renderer.c b/src/vrend/vrend_renderer.c
index b929846e131e97b7136c584d8113509c8ac494c4..ef0e44ed939753a4cbf31153d1d77505cae85615 100644
--- a/src/vrend/vrend_renderer.c
+++ b/src/vrend/vrend_renderer.c
@@ -2810,6 +2810,20 @@ int vrend_create_sampler_view(struct vrend_context *ctx,
       view->u.tex.last_layer = (val0 >> 16) & 0xffff;
       view->u.tex.first_level = val1 & 0xff;
       view->u.tex.last_level = (val1 >> 8) & 0xff;
+
+      /* A guest resource that is the second or a later plane of an image
+       * sends its plane number where the layers go, which no layer range can
+       * be, because the first layer would be past the last. Only a resource
+       * that holds the planes of an image has anything to select with it. A
+       * plane that has a resource of its own, as when the guest takes the
+       * planes from separate buffers, is the whole texture, and asking for
+       * layers that do not exist would fail the view and the command buffer
+       * with it.
+       */
+      if (view->u.tex.first_layer > view->u.tex.last_layer &&
+          !(val0 < ARRAY_SIZE(res->aux_plane_egl_image) &&
+            res->aux_plane_egl_image[val0]))
+         view->u.tex.first_layer = view->u.tex.last_layer = 0;
    }
 
    view->srgb_decode = GL_DECODE_EXT;
